# Present ONLY to stop npm falling back to .gitignore.
#
# `package.json#files` is already an allowlist, but npm still applies
# .gitignore to files INSIDE an included directory — and `dist/` is ignored
# there (correctly: build output does not belong in git). That combination
# would silently strip `plugins/c4s-plugin-api-contracts/dist` from the tarball,
# and a published host with no envelope loses the `endpoint` and `dto` types
# without an error: `discoverBuiltinEnvelopes()` just returns [].
#
# An .npmignore takes precedence over .gitignore, so this file being empty of
# rules means "exclude nothing beyond what `files` already excludes". Do not add
# rules here — narrow `files` instead, so there is one allowlist, not two.
